  "question": "What does a hit that breaks a Bursa's shields show, over its armored health?",
  "bible": "§15",
  "gameVersion": "44.1.4.1",
  "reports": [
    {
      "on": "2026-11-26",
      "words": "A Denial Bursa.\n| Level | White: on the shield | White: on health | Yellow: on the shield | Yellow: on health |\n| 10 | 7046 | 218 | 14028 | 485 |\n| 20 | 7137 | 138 | 14119 | 383 |"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Asked for in the Simulacrum with AI paused, Steel Path off, a fresh Bursa for every shot, the T-46 Lanka build (Serration, Radiated Reload, Primed Bane of Corpus, Stormbringer, Hellfire, Critical Delay, all at max), charged and unscoped at the middle of its body from about 10 m, and no numbers were predicted to Pavel. The shield shows the hit less 5% of the rest, as the shield took it: 7,345 less 5% of 7,345 − 3,193 at level 20 is 7,137, and health, under 372.9 armor, 138. Less the number on health, it would have shown 7,207. All eight numbers fit the wiki's Denial Bursa (1,200 health, 700 shields, 200 armor), whole shields (1,369 and 3,193) and its armor (246.8 and 372.9). The fixture brings the Denial Bursa with its body alone, the part the test hit, and Lanka's charged shot with Radiated Reload, for the reason in T-38.",
